{% icon id="banknote" size=32 /%}Storage full of loot you never wear? The Sell stored equipment {% term id="plugin" %}plugin{% /term %} sells loose equipment and gems from your storage, a few at a time.

Use it when your storage fills up with equipment and gems you don't need.

## How it works {% #how-it-works %}

1. After your bot signs in, it waits the number of minutes in **Minutes to wait after login before selling**, plus up to 3 minutes more.
2. It reads the equipment and the gems in your storage.
3. It sells up to **Items sold per run** items, one at a time, with a short pause between sales. Equipment comes first, then gems.
4. It waits about 5 minutes, then starts again at step 2.

Your {% term id="log" %}log{% /term %} shows how many pieces of equipment and how many gems each round sold.

## What the bot sells and keeps {% #what-it-sells %}

The bot sells:

- Equipment of every rarity except relic and unique. That includes epic and legendary pieces.
- Gems from your storage.

The bot never sells:

- Relic equipment.
- Unique equipment.
- Any piece of equipment or any gem that belongs to a set.

The bot sells only from storage.

{% aside type="caution" id="sales-are-final" %}
A sale cannot be undone. Before you turn the plugin on, check your storage. Anything there that is not relic, unique or part of a set gets sold.
{% /aside %}

## Settings {% #settings %}

{% settings plugin="sellStoredEquipment" /%}

**Minutes to wait after login before selling** sets how long the bot waits after it signs in before the first sale. The range is 1 to 60 minutes.

**Items sold per run** is how many items one round sells, from 1 to 50.

## Tips and limits {% #tips %}

- The plugin has no list of items to keep. Every stored item that is not relic, unique or part of a set is for sale.
- Turn the plugin off when you want to keep new loot for a while.

## Related errors {% #errors %}

If a number is outside its range when you save, the app shows [PLUGIN_OPTION_RANGE](/errors/#plugin-option-range).
